<title>UK: LucasVarity buys back more shares.</title>
<headline>LucasVarity buys back more shares.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-American engineering giant LucasVarity Plc said on Tuesday it had bought back 1.0 million of its ordinary shares at 184p per share as part of its share repurchase plan.</p>
<p>The company said it bought the shares, which represented about 0.07 percent of its ordinary share capital, from Cazenove &amp; Co.</p>
<p>LucasVarity's shares closed on Tuesday unchanged at 184 pence.</p>
<p>In April, the firm launched a programme to buy back 80 million stg of shares as part of its efforts to satisfy investors on both sides of the Atlantic.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
